---
/*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright Corsinvest Srl
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 *
 * What a cv4pve tool built on the Proxmox VE API needs from the sandbox of an AI assistant, and
 * the settings for Claude Code and Codex, for the page "AI assistants".
 *
 * Verified against cv4pve-api-dotnet v9.2.x: UpdateHelper.cs (daily release check on api.github.com,
 * cached in ~/.cv4pve/update-check.json, every failure ignored). Claude Code keys verified on
 * code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference (allowedDomains takes IP literals and `:port`,
 * allowMachLookup is an array of service names) and sandboxing (macOS, Linux and WSL2 only; a
 * `WebFetch(domain:…)` allow rule also pre-allows the host). Codex: `decision = "allow"` runs the
 * command outside the sandbox without prompting (learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/rules).
 * The trustd lookup was reported for cv4pve-cli (issue #10), which uses the same API library.
 * No headings here: Starlight builds "On this page" from the page's own headings only.
 */
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

interface Props {
  /** Tool binary, e.g. `cv4pve-report`. */
  tool: string;
  /** What the tool keeps in `~/.cv4pve/` and cannot run without, e.g. for cv4pve-cli. Unset: nothing. */
  config?: string;
}

const { tool, config } = Astro.props;

const claude = {
  sandbox: {
    network: { allowedDomains: ['pve01.example.com:8006'] },
    ...(config ? { filesystem: { allowWrite: ['~/.cv4pve/'] } } : {}),
  },
};
const trustd = { sandbox: { network: { allowMachLookup: ['com.apple.trustd*'] } } };
const codex = `prefix_rule(pattern=["${tool}"], decision="allow")`;
---

<p>{tool} needs to reach the nodes on port 8006, or the port in <code>--host</code>, and to write its output files.
Once a day it also asks <code>api.github.com</code> for a newer release: refusing that host only hides the notice.</p>

{config && <p>It also needs to write in <code>~/.cv4pve/</code>: {config}.</p>}

<p>
  Claude Code sandboxes commands on macOS, Linux and WSL2; on native Windows it has none, and the assistant runs
  commands with your own permissions. A Codex rule that allows {tool} runs it outside the sandbox. Either way the
  token is the only limit.
</p>

<details>
  <summary>Settings for Claude Code and Codex</summary>

  <p>
    <strong>Claude Code</strong> asks the first time a command reaches a new host. To allow the node in advance:
  </p>

  <Code code={JSON.stringify(claude, null, 2)} lang="json" title=".claude/settings.json" />

  <p>
    On macOS, with the self-signed certificate of the nodes, a cv4pve-cli user found in
    <a href="https://github.com/Corsinvest/cv4pve-cli/issues/10">issue #10</a> that the sandbox blocked every HTTPS
    connection, even with certificate validation off: .NET still asks the macOS trust service. {tool} connects
    with the same library, so the same fix may be needed:
  </p>

  <Code code={JSON.stringify(trustd, null, 2)} lang="json" title=".claude/settings.json" />

  <p><strong>Codex</strong>, in the same issue, needed only a rule that allows the command:</p>

  <Code code={codex} lang="text" title="~/.codex/rules/default.rules" />

  <p>
    Check these settings against the documentation of your assistant —
    <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing">Claude Code</a>,
    <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/rules">Codex</a>.
  </p>
</details>
